* =====================================================================================================
* sleep_current__nrf52840.lib -- nRF52840 (Raytac MDBT50Q-U1MV2) System ON idle + GPIO pin states, DC model
*
* Part      : Nordic nRF52840 in the Raytac MDBT50Q-U1MV2 module (main board U10), normal-voltage mode,
*             VDD = VDDH = +3V3
* Datasheet : nRF52840 Product Specification v1.1 (4413_417 v1.1),
*             https://infocenter.nordicsemi.com/pdf/nRF52840_PS_v1.1.pdf
*
* Core current (subckt SC_NRF52840_SYSON, VDD -> GND):
*   ION = ION_RAMON_RTC - ILFRC + ILFXO = 3.16 - 0.70 + 0.23 = 2.69 uA
*         ION_RAMON_RTC 3.16 uA typ: System ON, full 256 kB RAM retention, wake on RTC (LFRC)  (§5.2.1.1)
*         ILFRC 0.7 uA run current (§5.4.4.4); ILFXO 0.23 uA run current (§5.4.4.3):
*         this board runs the RTC from the 32.768 kHz crystal Y1, so the LFRC share is swapped for the LFXO.
*   + ISENSE = ION_RAMON_GPIOTEPORT - ION_RAMON_EVENT = 2.36 - 2.35 = 0.01 uA for the PORT/SENSE wake pins
*   Supply slope: +8.3 %/V around 3 V (Figure 10, 25 C curve: about 1.00 uA at 3.0 V, 1.05 uA at 3.6 V).
*   Temperature: factor read off Figure 10 (System ON, no RAM retention, typical): 0.30 at -40 C, 1.0 at 25 C,
*         10.4 at 85 C, interpolated log-linearly; applied to the whole ION (conservative: LFXO/RTC part is
*         less temperature dependent). -10 C -> x0.52, 60 C -> x3.92.
*   The PS gives typical values only (no maximum), so MAXC is accepted but unused. Test conditions are 3 V,
*   LDO regulator; this board uses REG1 DC/DC, which does not change the sleep figures materially.
*
* GPIO pin states (subckts below, one per pin, connected between the pin net, VDD and GND):
*   OUT_LOW / OUT_HIGH  standard drive: VOL/VOH within 0.4 V at 0.5 mA (§6.9.3.1 VOL,SD /
*                       VOH,SD) -> 800 ohm to the rail (worst-case output resistance; sleep loads are uA)
*   PULLUP / PULLDOWN   RPU / RPD 13 kohm typ (11-16 kohm, §6.9.3.1)
*   HIGHZ               input (SENSE, no pull), disconnected, or analog: no DC element. The PS gives no
*                       input-leakage figure, so none is modelled.
*
* Supply currents are scaled by tanh(V/50 mV) so that they vanish on an unpowered rail (ship mode).
* NOT modelled: radio, CPU wake-ups and RTC interrupt service (System ON idle only), SAADC sampling every
*   10 min (firmware §12.3), errata currents (anomaly 89 / 195), USB regulator (VBUS absent on battery),
*   DCCH. NFCT: since the 2026-10-19 netlist P0.09/P0.10 carry an NFC antenna (NFC1/NFC2, coil on J11, C16/C17
*   to GND; nets.py: UICR NFCPINS left in NFC mode). With NFCT disabled there is no DC path; if firmware arms
*   NFCT field SENSE in sleep add Isense 100 nA typ (PS v1.1 §5.2.1.4) -- firmware.md does not define it yet.
*   INFC_LEAK (1 / 10 uA, §6.9.3.1) applies only in GPIO mode with the pads at different levels. [verifier]
* =====================================================================================================
.subckt SC_NRF52840_SYSON vdd vss params: TEMP=25 MAXC=0
.param ion = {3.16u - 0.70u + 0.23u + (2.36u - 2.35u)}
.param kt  = {TEMP >= 25 ? pow(10.4, (TEMP - 25)/60) : pow(0.30, (25 - TEMP)/65)}
Bcore vdd vss I = 'ion * kt * (1 + 0.083*(v(vdd,vss) - 3.0)) * tanh(v(vdd,vss)/0.05)'
.ends SC_NRF52840_SYSON

.subckt SC_NRF_GPIO_OUT_LOW pin vdd vss
Rdrv pin vss 800
.ends SC_NRF_GPIO_OUT_LOW

.subckt SC_NRF_GPIO_OUT_HIGH pin vdd vss
Rdrv vdd pin 800
.ends SC_NRF_GPIO_OUT_HIGH

.subckt SC_NRF_GPIO_PULLUP pin vdd vss
Rpu vdd pin 13k
.ends SC_NRF_GPIO_PULLUP

.subckt SC_NRF_GPIO_PULLDOWN pin vdd vss
Rpd pin vss 13k
.ends SC_NRF_GPIO_PULLDOWN
